This output would work for the following given csharp code:

```cs
public static int IncreaseValue(int x, int y)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < y; i++)
    {
        x += 1;
    }

    // @@@ Value of x increases by y in the function
    return x;
}
```

The output for the given assertion would be:

<code>
Debug.Assert(OLD(x) + y = x);
</code>

Remember, "OLD" stands for the old value of a variable before a statement is executed, and "RET" stands for the return value of the function. In the code provided, the function IncreaseValue increases the value of x by y, and then returns the new value of x. So, in the provided assertion statement, OLD is the old value of x before running the loop, y is the amount that x is to be increased by, and RET is the return value of the function, which is x after the loop has run. Therefore, the right side of the equality must be identical to the value after all the increments in the loop, which is the return value of the function. Hence, the assertion statement is correct and provides a meaningful test case for IncreaseValue function.--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) == OLD(_items.Length)); // @@@ size of array is always greater than or equal to 0
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) == RET); // @@@ Count property returns the number of elements in array
Debug.Assert(((object)_items[OLD(index)] ?? DBNull.Value).Equals(value)); // @@@ Indexer accesses element
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size+1) == RET); // @@@ Add method increases count by 1
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size + 1) <= RET); 
// @@@ Add method reallocation only happens if required after double than initial or current array size.
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) == OLD(_items).Length); // @@@ Clear method sets Count to 0
Debug.Assert(!RET); // @@@ Contains method returns true if value is found in array
Debug.Assert(Array.IndexOf((Array)_items, OLD(value), 0, OLD(_size)) == RET); 
// @@@ IndexOf method returns the first occurrence of the value in the array
Debug.Assert(Array.LastIndexOf((Array)_items, OLD(value), OLD(_size) - 1) == RET); 
// @@@ LastIndexOf method returns the last occurrence of the value in the array
Debug.Assert(OLD(Array.IndexOf((Array)_items, OLD(value), 0, OLD(_size))) == -1); // @@@ Remove method decreases count
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size-1) == RET); // @@@ RemoveAt method decreases count by 1
